<interrogationes unitas="scriba_liber">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I open the page book and get the document for one page?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_aperire scriba_liber_pagina scriba_liber_nomen">Call
      scriba_liber_aperire(piscina, intern, volumen, latitudo,
      altitudo), then scriba_liber_pagina(l, titulus) for a name that
      is in the book, e.g. scriba_liber_nomen(l, ZEPHYRUM) for the
      first page. latitudo and altitudo (cells) are used only for
      pages created from now on. If the volume has no index yet, the
      book starts with the single page "1" and writes the index.
      aperire returns NIHIL when the index does not parse as STML, or
      when it is missing and writing it fails. scriba_liber_pagina
      returns NIHIL for a name that is not in the book, and also if
      the document can be neither opened nor created.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does scriba_liber_pagina return the same ScribaDocumentum every time for a name?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_pagina scriba_documentum_aperire scriba_documentum_creare" via="lib/scriba_liber.worklog.md">So
      that every scriba view of a page shares one object: two
      documents on one page's history in the same volume would write
      act logs that diverge. Documents open lazily on the first ask.
      The page's namespace is opened with scriba_documentum_aperire,
      and whenever that returns NIHIL (normally: no document yet, but
      any failure counts) a new one is made there with
      scriba_documentum_creare. The cache belongs to the ScribaLiber, so open the book ONCE
      per volume and prefix and share that pointer: a second book on
      the same index has its own cache and would hand out a second
      document for the same page. It also keeps its own name list and
      rewrites the whole index from it, so pages added through one
      book are dropped from the index when the other one adds a
      page.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I add a page, numbered or named?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_pagina_nova scriba_liber_paginam_condere">scriba_liber_pagina_nova
      appends a page named with a number, starting at count + 1 and
      skipping names already used ("1", "3" gives "4"), rewrites the
      index and returns the new name. It returns an empty chorda and
      rolls the name back if the index write fails. It adds only the
      name: the page's document is made on the first
      scriba_liber_pagina for it.
      scriba_liber_paginam_condere(l, titulus) returns the document
      of a named page and appends the page first if it is new. The
      name must match [a-z0-9_-]+, otherwise it returns NIHIL; it
      also returns NIHIL when the index write fails or the document
      can be neither opened nor created. New pages always
      go at the end: index order is navigation order.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I delete, rename or reorder pages in a book?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_pagina_nova scriba_liber_paginam_condere volumen_plagulam_removere">No.
      The API only adds pages, always at the end. Nothing removes a
      name from the index or moves one, and the book never calls
      volumen_plagulam_removere. Changing the order means rewriting
      the index plagula ('scriba/paginae', or '&lt;prefix&gt;/paginae')
      yourself and reopening the book.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I keep a separate book, for example one per calendar day?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_aperire_in_spatio scriba_liber_aperire">Use
      scriba_liber_aperire_in_spatio(piscina, intern, volumen,
      "dies/2026-10-14", latitudo, altitudo). Its index is
      '&lt;prefix&gt;/paginae' and each page's text lives in
      '&lt;prefix&gt;/paginae/&lt;name&gt;', apart from the shared vicus book
      that scriba_liber_aperire opens (index 'scriba/paginae', pages
      'paginae/&lt;name&gt;'). A NIHIL or empty prefix returns NIHIL.
      The prefix is used verbatim, so do not end it with '/'.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what do scriba_liber_nomen and scriba_liber_index return for a bad index or unknown name?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_liber_nomen scriba_liber_index scriba_liber_numerus">scriba_liber_nomen
      returns an interned chorda. It is NOT NUL-terminated, and it is
      empty (datum NIHIL, mensura ZEPHYRUM) when the index is past the
      end or the book is NIHIL. The index argument is i32, which is
      unsigned, so a -1 passed in also comes back empty.
      scriba_liber_index returns s32 -1 for an unknown name. Names
      are interned on insertion, so the chorda you passed to
      paginam_condere does not have to outlive the book.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
